⚖️ TODAY ON CAPITOL HILL: The American Bar Association should not have a government-backed monopoly over legal education while pushing a partisan ideological agenda.

Law school accreditation should uphold the Constitution, protect equal treatment under the law, and serve students, not force radical DEI mandates onto America’s future lawyers.

@tzsmith is a Senior Legal Fellow of Courts and the Constitution at The Heritage Foundation.

TODAY ON CAPITOL HILL: The Abraham Accords weren't a diplomatic miracle. They were the result of bold American leadership and a willingness to challenge the status quo.

Expanding these agreements can strengthen regional security, advance economic cooperation, and create new opportunities for peace and prosperity.

@fredman_a is a Visiting Fellow in the Allison Center for National Security at The Heritage Foundation.

TODAY ON CAPITOL HILL: 🚢 America needs a "SpaceX moment" for shipbuilding.

The future of maritime power won't be built through bureaucracy. It will be built through innovation, investment, and a renewed commitment to American industry. It's time to restore our maritime strength and secure our nation's future.

@brentdsadler is a Senior Research Fellow for Naval Warfare and Advanced Technology in the Allison Center for National Security at The Heritage Foundation.

